  "_liveStateNote": "REFERENCE COPY -- n8n is the source of truth; this file is documentation. Exported from the live instance September 3, 2026 and mirrored again the same evening after the id fix. THIS IS THE WORKFLOW EVERY OTHER WORKFLOW NAMES IN ITS Error Workflow FIELD. It had no copy in this repo until September 3, which is why a session reading only the collector concluded that was the error mechanism and wrote the wiring instruction naming it; n8n allows one error workflow per workflow and this is the one that was set. FIXED AND VERIFIED September 3, 2026: the first export mapped the column id with a literal 0 on an INSERT into a bigserial PRIMARY KEY, so the first row took id=0 and every later error would have died on a duplicate key -- silently, because the Telegram node runs in parallel and keeps working. id is now unmapped, occurred_at stays unmapped, and two consecutively forced errors produced ids 1 and 2. DO NOT re-add id or occurred_at to the mapping: both are database-generated."
